7le18ob01re2img03.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn7le18ob01re2img03.jpg"}, {"text": "People have been growing rice for food in Eastern Asia for thousands of years. It has become the staff of life for half the nations in the world. It has come to be so important to the Chinese that, \"Have you eaten your rice today?\" has emerged as a greeting similar to, \"How are you?\".", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn7le18ob01re2img03.jpg"}, {"text": "Farmers have been cultivating rice in the U.S. in Virginia for 400 years. Since then, this practice has spread to other states. In the past hundred years, half of the rice consumed in the U.S. has been grown there.", "id": 2, "time": "17000", "image": "engenn7le18ob01re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "I read in the newspaper that in North America our tastes have been changing in the past quarter century. Dishes from Asia have been turning up in ethnic restaurants and Fusion Cuisine.", "id": 3, "time": "29000", "image": "engenn7le18ob01re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "A friend, who is a chef, tells me that different types of rice have been appearing in supermarkets in the past decade. More, she emphasizes, keep coming. She has been experimenting for the last few months with a few of the myriad of varieties that have been popping up. Since people have been shifting toward healthier, lighter foods, she tells me, the consumption of rice has risen.", "id": 4, "time": "38500", "image": "engenn7le18ob01re2img02.jpg"}]}}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Rice Cookout"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Cashing in Rice"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 18}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect Continuous vs. Present Perfect"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You use the<span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about an unspecified time in the past that is related to now or continues up to now.</p>When you use the Present Perfect tense, the time when the action happened is not important.<br/>When you use the Present Perfect Continuous tense, the time when the action happened is also not important."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about:<ul><li>experience up to the present</li><li>change that has happened over time</li><li>an event or action that happened in the past that is important now</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the<span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect Continuous</span>:<ul><li>to emphasize that action has continued without stopping until now and may still be taking place</li><li>when you can see the result of an action that happened in the recent past</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span>: <span class=\"italic\">I have made dinner.</span> (dinner is ready to eat)<br/><span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect Continuous</span>: <span class=\"italic\">I have been making dinner.</span> (I am still working on it or I just finished right now)"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Perfect tense</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Perfect Continuous tense</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>Rice <span class=\\\"strong\\\">has become</span> the staff of life for half the nations in the world. </p><p>For the past hundred years, half of the rice consumed in the U.S. <span class=\\\"strong\\\">has grown</span> there.</p><p>In North America our tastes<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> have changed </span> in the past quarter century.</p></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>People <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have been growing</span> rice for food in Eastern Asia for thousands of years.</p><p>Farmers <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have been cultivating </span>rice in the U.S. in Virginia for 400 years.</p><p>Dishes from Asia <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have been turning up </span> in ethnic restaurants and Fusion Cuisine. </p></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Since</span>, <span class=\"italic\">For</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">In</span> for Duration"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span> and the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect Continuous tense</span>, you often use phrases or clauses for duration."}, {"type": "text", "content": "These phrases or clauses begin with <span class=\"italic\">for</span>, <span class=\"italic\">in</span> or <span class=\"italic\">since</span>. They answer the question \u201cHow long ... ?\u201d."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">since</span> to begin a phrase or a clause (as a connector or as a preposition)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">for</span> and <span class=\"italic\">in</span> to begin a phrase (as a preposition)."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Preposition</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"for (the total amount of time)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">for thousands of years<br/>for the past few months<br/>for 400 years</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"since (from the point in time that it started)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">since then<br/>since January<br/>since 2010</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in (inside that period of time)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">in the past decade<br/>in the past hundred years</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Connector</span></div>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"since (from the point in time that it started)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Since people have been shifting toward healthier, lighter foods ...</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Since people have been shifting toward healthier, lighter foods, she tells me, the consumption of rice has risen."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Since then this practice has spread to other states. In the past hundred years, half of the rice consumed in the U.S has grown there."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Farmers have been cultivating rice in the U.S. in Virginia for 400 years."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This means Americans have burned more rice in the past decade than any other people in the whole world!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "the staff of life"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a necessary food; a staple food"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In China, rice is the staff of life."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about rice."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to emerge"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to come out, to appear"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: \u201cHave you eaten your rice today?\" has emerged as a greeting in China."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to cultivate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to grow on a farm"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Farmers have been cultivating rice in the U.S. in Virginia for 400 years."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "demographic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "groups in a population"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The demographic in North America has been changing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ethnic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "from a specific place and group of people"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This city has a wide variety of ethnic restaurants."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "Fusion Cuisine"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "cooking that combines food traditions from different cultures in contemporary restaurants"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This restaurant is famous for its Fusion Cuisine."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob01aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to transform"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to change"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The demographic in North America has been constantly transforming."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob01aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "myriad"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large number"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are a myriad of choices when it comes to rice."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob01aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to appear"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to show up; to become noticeable"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: New types of rice are appearing in supermarkets"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le18ob01aud08"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le18ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Talk with your partner about the types of food you have tried."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a report on how your eating habits have changed."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Identify a type of food that has become popular in your country and why you have or have not tried it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your report to a partner and discuss it. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I discuss food I have tried."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about food that has become popular."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss how my eating habits have changed."}]}], "type": "sena"}